The Audi SQ5 Plus Special Edition is based on the first generation SQ5, specifically the diesel BiTDI version, and was available around 2016-2017. It was a limited run model.

**Key Specs Found:**
*   **Engine:** 3.0L BiTDI V6
*   **Power:** 340 PS (335-340 hp)
*   **Torque:** 516 lb-ft (700 Nm)
*   **0-60 mph:** 4.9 - 5.1 seconds (Using 5.0 as average)
*   **Top Speed:** 155 mph (limited)
*   **Transmission:** 8-speed Tiptronic automatic
*   **Drive Type:** Quattro (All-wheel drive)
*   **MPG (Combined NEDC):** 42.8 mpg (Real world likely lower, around 20-30 mpg based on general SQ5 data) - Will use a score based on the official figure relative to other performance SUVs of its era, but acknowledge it's a diesel.
*   **CO2:** 174 g/km
*   **Price (when new):** Around £51,845 - £53,200 (Convert to USD for scoring - £52,500 is roughly $66,500 USD as of mid-2024 exchange rates, but this was a 2016 car, so the original USD price would have been different. Using current conversion for scoring relative to today's market average).
*   **Insurance Group (UK):** 45E (High group)
*   **Cargo Space:** 540L (seats up) (Convert to cu ft: 540 L * 0.0353147 = ~19.07 cu ft)
*   **Seats:** 5
*   **Body Style:** SUV/Estate (5-door)
*   **Wheelbase:** 2813 mm (~110.7 inches)
*   **Length:** 4629-4644 mm (~182 inches)
*   **Width (inc. mirrors):** 2089 mm (~82 inches)
*   **Height (inc. roof rails):** 1624 mm (~64 inches)
*   **Ground Clearance:** Not explicitly stated, but being an SQ5 with lowered suspension (30mm lower than standard Q5), it's lower than a standard SUV. Estimate around 6 inches or slightly less.
*   **Turn Radius:** 11.7 m (~38.4 ft)
*   **Electrification:** Diesel (ICE)
*   **Interior:** Quilted Nappa leather, Bang & Olufsen sound system, MMI Navigation Plus, Virtual Cockpit (on some later models/packages), panoramic sunroof, heated/power/massage seats (on Special Edition/options). Interior design is noted as aging compared to newer Audis.
*   **Handling/Ride:** Sporty but firm ride, especially at low speeds. Good grip, capable handling for an SUV, but steering can feel light/vague. Optional sport differential improves agility. Comfortable on highways.
*   **Visibility:** Noted as terrible due to large wing mirrors.
*   **ADAS:** Adaptive cruise control, parking assist, blind spot monitoring, etc. available/standard on later models/Special Edition.
*   **Reliability:** Generally considered reasonably reliable for a German luxury car, but not Honda/Toyota levels. Potential issues mentioned include brake wear, oil consumption, transmission failure (rare). Maintenance costs are higher than non-performance models.

